<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01524#violent_retaliation_stereotype> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The meme relies on the stereotype that individuals, particularly men, may resort to extreme violence (e.g., pulling out a gun) as a response to perceived betrayal or infidelity. This reflects a harmful cultural trope that normalizes or trivializes the use of lethal force in personal relationships, which can be dangerous and is often associated with toxic masculinity."@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#metaphoricallyMapsTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#relatesTo> .
