<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01524#mapping_001> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The text 'when you catch your goat with another man' implies that the person depicted (the 'goat') is the romantic partner who has been unfaithful. The visual material of the person holding a concealed weapon is mapped onto this textual role, suggesting that this individual is the one who has been caught in infidelity. The mapping is established through the juxtaposition of the text and the visual, where the person's threatening posture and weapon symbolize the violent retaliation expected from the 'goat' being caught. This is an analogical mapping where the visual entity (person) is projected as the textual entity ('goat') in the context of betrayal."@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#Toxicity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Toxicity Assessment includes: harmful elements, offensive content, toxic indicators, problematic elements, negative aspects, and harmful signals."@en .
