<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#underpinsCosmicIronyOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Indicates text highlighting the absurdity or ironic nature of the visual situation in memes"@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#OverallIntent> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#promptExtractionText> "Extract Overall Intent elements from the image. Overall Intent includes: communicative purposes, creator intentions, message goals, intended effects, purpose indicators, and intent signals. For each intentional element found, provide: 1) A descriptive instance_name (e.g., 'humor_intent', 'social_commentary'), 2) A natural language label (e.g., 'the humor intent', 'the social commentary'), 3) A brief description of the intended purpose or effect. Focus on what the meme creator likely intended to communicate or achieve. Example output format: {\"instance_name\": \"humor_intent\", \"label\": \"the humor intent\", \"description\": \"The meme appears designed to create humor through the contrast between the girl's calm expression and the chaotic fire scene\"}"@en .
_:neaf6236668de4515a50e7bd4bdc8f68db61 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#unionOf> _:neaf6236668de4515a50e7bd4bdc8f68db62 .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01524#overallintent_instance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "meme-id: meme_file_name; hasOverallIntent: overall-intent_id; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a person in casual attire (black hoodie and jeans) holding a handgun, with the text overlay 'when you catch your goat with another man.' The scene is framed to focus on the weapon and the act of concealment, suggesting a violent or retaliatory response. The overall intent is to convey a humorous or exaggerated threat in response to infidelity, using the visual of a gun to symbolize extreme, dangerous consequences. This meme relies on the juxtaposition of the mundane (a 'goat' as a metaphor for a partner) with the violent (a gun), creating a darkly comedic effect. While the meme is not explicitly abusive, hateful, or propagandistic toward specific groups, it contains harmful content by normalizing or trivializing the use of violence as a response to betrayal. The presence of the weapon, combined with the context of infidelity, can be seen as promoting a culture of aggression and potentially dangerous behavior, which may be harmful to individuals or communities that perceive such threats as realistic or justified. The meme does not target any specific protected characteristic (race, gender, etc.) but rather uses a universal metaphor for betrayal, making it less cyberbullying or misogynistic in nature, though its underlying message of violence is inherently harmful."@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#NarrativeFlowAdjacency> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
