<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01524#toxic_masculinity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The meme implicitly references the concept of toxic masculinity, which is a social and cultural phenomenon where men are expected to suppress emotions, assert dominance, and resort to aggression or violence to resolve personal conflicts, especially those involving relationships and perceived betrayal. This concept is central to understanding why the meme is framed as a 'threat' rather than a humorous or exaggerated joke."@en .
